0..70 Comment "// Vector programs as they should read, and what refuses each of them."
71..73 Comment "//"
74..153 Comment "// A case on a vector binds each arm\'s index equation, prunes an arm whose ends"
154..232 Comment "// are apart, and solves an equation with a variable side. An equation between"
233..301 Comment "// two applications of one constructor stays unsolved. A binder of a"
302..342 Comment "// recursion\'s stage is not generalised."
343..345 Comment "//"
346..417 Comment "// The checker refuses each declaration below by the name its attribute"
418..496 Comment "// states. Each turns to `checks` as its rung lands, and the source then moves"
497..518 Comment "// to the model root."
519..521 Comment "//"
522..603 Comment "// - see: #3627 — not implemented: a constructor at an index written as a call,"
604..621 Comment "//   for `append`"
622..692 Comment "// - see: #3631 — not implemented: a transport\'s motive that names a"
693..726 Comment "//   recursion\'s stage, for `zip`"
727..797 Comment "// - see: #3515 — not implemented: injectivity, for `tail` and `zip`"
798..871 Comment "// - see: #3516 — not implemented: an implicit under a constructor, for"
872..890 Comment "//   `firstOfPair`"
891..969 Comment "// - see: #3517 — not implemented: an implicit block on `def rec`, for `zip`"
970..987 Comment "//   and `append`"
988..1043 Comment "// - see: #3481 — the spike that wrote these programs"
1045..1082 Comment "// The naturals the lengths count in."
